  "id": "Compound::DB00705 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Delavirdine, a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is linked to Cyp2c9 through its inclusion in the class of non-nucleoside analogs and its association with Efavirenz, a member of this class. Both Delavirdine and Efavirenz bind to Cyp2c9, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the cytochrome P450 2C9 enzyme. The lowest common ancestor of Delavirdine and Efavirenz is the organic heterobicyclic compound, reinforcing the structural and functional relationship between these entities. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Delavirdine and Cyp2c9, likely through the inhibition of the enzyme, which is further supported by the presence of Efavirenz in the same class. The relationship is further illuminated by the fact that Delavirdine may contribute to Cyp2c9 activity through its inclusion in the same class as Efavirenz, highlighting a potential pathway where the non-nucleoside inhibitor class influences enzyme activity.",
